{
  "_why": [
    "Routes that moved. Every entry keeps a URL that was published and indexed",
    "resolving after a chapter changed owners.",
    "`from` is the route as it was served, without the /playground/ baseUrl --",
    "the plugin prepends it. `to` must resolve in the current build or the build",
    "fails, which is the point: a redirect that rots is worse than none.",
    "Append here when a chapter moves; never delete an entry, because the old",
    "URL stays in somebody's history forever.",
    "",
    "`legacyPrefixes` is the same promise for whole trees that moved as one:",
    "every current route under `to` also resolves under `from` with the same",
    "suffix. The missions/ level was removed and the remaining directories were",
    "pulled up one level; infra/ was absorbed into the topic that uses the",
    "mechanism. docusaurus.config.ts derives the per-route redirects from this",
    "list, longest `to` first so a vision route matches the vision entry before",
    "the language-model entry it is nested under."
  ],
